{
 "elemod": 2,
 "id": "machines",
 "version": "0.6",
 "title": "machines",
 "description": "Machines for the Digitone mk1 and Digitone Keys: sounds that play a machine mod's voice in place of FM, through the Digitone's own filter, mixer and effects, with the AMP page's envelope. MACHINES in core-dn1's Mod Menu (hold a track key) picks the held track's machine; a machine track's SYN1 and SYN2 knobs are the machine's parameters, relabelled, and from 0.2 their second pages too for a machine that takes them (27 knobs). On its own it adds the menu and nothing else: machines come in mods of their own. From 0.3 also the SDK alpha's machines, whose page replaces SYN2's pages on their tracks, and from 0.4 a voice's count of the silent frames it was not rendered (idle), and from 0.5 mono machines (.pick), one key and one voice at a time on their tracks. Needs core-dn1 5.2 (0.2: 3.1; the 1.44 port from 0.5, 5.3).",
 "category": "Framework",
 "author": "irpina",
 "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
 "target": {
  "device": "digitone-mk1",
  "product": "Digitone mk1",
  "os": "1.44",
  "syx_sha256": "d4f200d04484333d82822db7744e6484d0def8f2db8ddf55ee2b780cc13c9659",
